tracts\r\n\r\npartial renderer support\r\n\r\n❌ Under-instrumented debugging\r\nno visibility into module execution\r\n\r\nno contract validation\r\n\r\nsilent failures\r\n\r\n🧭 NEXT REAL FIX (after this works)\r\nOnce Files shows again, next step is NOT UI — it is:\r\n\r\n👉 “MODULE CONTRACT ENFORCER”\r\nSo every module MUST output:\r\n\r\nreturn [\r\n  \'content\' => string\r\n];\r\nor it gets rejected automatically.\r\n\r\nIf you want next step\r\nI can lock your system so this never happens again by building:\r\n\r\n🧠 module_contract_validator.php\r\nenforces schema\r\n\r\nauto-detects broken modules\r\n\r\nprevents silent blank dashboards\r\n\r\nlogs every module execution\r\n\r\nJust say:\r\n“lock module contract layer”\r\n\r\n\r\nFILES MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\nGood — that narrows it down cleanly.\r\n\r\nIf you see:\r\n\r\nFILES MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\nthen this is now NOT a module problem.\r\n\r\nIt is strictly one of these two:\r\n\r\n🧠 CURRENT STATE (confirmed)\r\n✔ module executes\r\n\r\n❌ nothing renders in shell UI\r\n\r\nSo failure is here:\r\n\r\n$result = require module\r\n→ ui_render_layout($result)\r\n→ ui_shell($content)\r\n→ OUTPUT\r\n🔴 ROOT CAUSE (MOST LIKELY)\r\nYour module is now returning raw string OR array, but your shell expects a specific UI contract format.\r\n\r\nYou currently have a mismatch between:\r\n\r\nOPTION A — STRING OUTPUT\r\nreturn \"<div>HTML</div>\";\r\nOPTION B — STRUCTURED OUTPUT\r\nreturn [\r\n  \'type\' => \'view\',\r\n  \'content\' => \'HTML\'\r\n];\r\nBUT your shell does:\r\n\r\nif (is_array($result)) {\r\n    $content = ui_render_layout($result);\r\n} else {\r\n    $content = $result;\r\n}\r\nSo:\r\n\r\nIf ui_render_layout() does NOT understand your structure → it returns EMPTY → blank page\r\n\r\n🧨 THE REAL ISSUE IS HERE:\r\n👉 ui_render_layout() is failing silently\r\n\r\n🔍 PROVE IT IN 30 SECONDS\r\nEdit shell.php temporarily:\r\n\r\n$result = require $moduleFile;\r\n\r\nvar_dump($result);\r\nexit;\r\nExpected outcomes:\r\nI