NLY remaining cause would be:\r\n\r\n❗ graph_module.php was accidentally pasted into files_module.php\r\n\r\nBut based on what you sent — that is NOT the case.\r\n\r\n🧭 EXPECTED RESULT\r\nYou now have:\r\n\r\n✔ correct routing\r\n✔ correct module loading\r\n✔ no cross-page contamination\r\n✔ stable rendering pipeline\r\n\r\n👉 NEXT STEP\r\nOnce confirmed:\r\n\r\n“modules loading correctly”\r\n\r\nWe move into:\r\n\r\n🔥 REAL graph system (node relationships + connections)\r\n\r\nThis is where your platform stops being a CMS and becomes actual intelligence software.\r\n\r\n\r\ngraph module=<?php\r\n\r\n$stmt = $pdo->query(\"\r\n    SELECT id, title, cluster_id\r\n    FROM page\r\n    ORDER BY created DESC\r\n    LIMIT 100\r\n\");\r\n\r\n$rows = $stmt->fetchAll();\r\n\r\n?>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-grid\">\r\n\r\n<?php foreach ($rows as $r): ?>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"service-card\">\r\n        <h3><?= htmlspecialchars($r[\'title\']) ?></h3>\r\n        <p>Cluster: <?= $r[\'cluster_id\'] ?? \'none\' ?></p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n<?php endforeach; ?>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\nGood — both modules you showed are clean and different, so we can rule out file mix-ups.\r\n\r\nThat leaves only one real cause:\r\n\r\nYour server is serving a cached/old version of shell.php (or opcode cache), not your updated one.\r\n\r\nBecause with the shell I gave you, it is impossible for Files to render Graph unless caching is involved.\r\n\r\n🧠 PROOF CHECK (DO THIS FIRST — VERY IMPORTANT)\r\nWe’re going to force a visible marker to confirm what file is actually being executed.\r\n\r\n📁 OPEN:\r\n/commandcenter/modules/files_module.php\r\n\r\nADD THIS AT THE VERY TOP (FIRST LINE AFTER <?php):\r\necho \"<div style=\'color:red;\'>FILES MODULE LOADED</div>\";\r\n📁 OPEN:\r\n/commandcenter/modules/graph_module.php\r\n\r\nADD THIS AT THE TOP:\r\necho \"<div style=\'color:lime;\'>GRAPH MODULE LOADED</div>\";\r\n🧪 NOW TEST\r\nGo to:\r\n/files.php\r\nYou should see:\r\n🔴 FILES MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\nGo to:\r\n/graph.php\r\nYou should see:\r\n🟢 GRAPH MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\n🚨 INTERPRET RESULTS\r\nCASE 1 — BOTH SHOW GRAPH MESSAGE\r\n→ ❌ Server is caching old file\r\n→ shell.php not updating\r\n\r\nCASE 2 — FILES SHOWS GRAPH MESSAGE\r\n→ ❌ Wrong module still being included (100% shell issue)\r\n\r\nCASE 3 — BOTH CORRECT\r\n→ ✔ system fixed, previous view was cached\r\n\r\n🧱 STEP 2 — FORCE CACHE RESET (VERY COMMON ON YOUR HOSTING)\r\nYou are on a stack that likely uses:\r\n\r\nOPcache\r\n\r\nserver-level caching\r\n\r\nQUICK FIX (DO THIS)\r\nOPTION A (FASTEST)\r\nAdd this at TOP of shell.php:\r\n\r\nopcache_reset();\r\nOPTION B (ALSO DO THIS)\r\nHard refresh browser:\r\n\r\nWindows: CTRL + F5\r\n\r\nMac: CMD + SHIFT + R\r\n\r\nOPTION C (NUCLEAR — GUARANTEED)\r\nRename file temporarily:\r\n\r\nshell.php → shell_v2.php\r\nThen update one page:\r\n\r\ninclude __DIR__ . \"/shell_v2.php\";\r\nIf it suddenly works → caching confirmed.\r\n\r\n🧠 WHY THIS IS HAPPENING\r\nYour logic is now correct.\r\n\r\nSo the only explanation left is:\r\n\r\nPHP is executing a previously compiled version of your file (opcode cache)\r\n\r\nThis is extremely common in shared hosting.\r\n\r\n🚀 AFTER THIS\r\nOnce confirmed working:\r\n\r\nREMOVE the debug lines:\r\n\r\necho \"FILES MODULE LOADED\";\r\necho \"GRAPH MODULE LOADED\";\r\n👉 NEXT STEP\r\nTell me what you saw:\r\n\r\n“files shows X / graph shows X”\r\n\r\nThen I’ll either:\r\n\r\nfinalize fix (if caching)\r\n\r\nor go one layer deeper (if something unexpected appears)\r\n\r\nWe are very close — this is the last routing-level issue.\r\n\r\n\r\nGRAPH MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\nPerfect — that result is decisive.\r\n\r\nFiles page is loading Graph module\r\nSo this is NOT caching.\r\nThis is NOT module content.\r\n\r\nThis is shell.php still loading the wrong file.\r\n\r\n🧠 ROOT CAUSE (FINAL, NO MORE GUESSING)\r\nEven though your pages set:\r\n\r\n$contentFile = __DIR__ . \"/modules/files_module.php\";\r\nYour shell.php is NOT using that variable correctly.\r\n\r\nEither:\r\n\r\nit’s being overwritten\r\n\r\nor there’s another include before/after\r\n\r\nor an old loader block still exists\r\n\r\n🧱 WE FIX THIS WITH A HARD OVERRIDE (NO AMBIGUITY)\r\nWe are going to force shell to derive module from the URL directly.\r\n\r\nThis removes ALL dependency on $contentFile.\r\n\r\n🧱 STEP — FULL shell.php REPLACEMENT (FINAL FIX)\r\n📁 OPEN:\r\n/commandcenter/shell.php\r\n✂️ DELETE EVERYTHING\r\n✅ REPLACE WITH THIS:\r\n<?php\r\nrequire_once __DIR__ . \"/bootstrap.php\";\r\n\r\n$pageTitle = $pageTitle ?? \"LEGAiSEE\";\r\n$pageDesc  = $pageDesc ?? \"\";\r\n\r\n$current = basename($_SERVER[\'PHP_SELF\']);\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   FORCE MODULE BY ROUTE\r\n--------------------------- */\r\nswitch ($current) {\r\n\r\n    case \'index.php\':\r\n        $module = __DIR__ . \"/modules/dashboard_module.php\";\r\n        break;\r\n\r\n    case \'search.php\':\r\n        $module = __DIR__ . \"/modules/search_module.php\";\r\n        break;\r\n\r\n    case \'ingest.php\':\r\n        $module = __DIR__ . \"/modules/ingest_module.php\";\r\n        break;\r\n\r\n    case \'files.php\':\r\n        $module = __DIR__ . \"/modules/files_module.php\";\r\n        break;\r\n\r\n    case \'graph.php\':\r\n        $module = __DIR__ . \"/modules/graph_module.php\";\r\n        break;\r\n\r\n    default:\r\n        $module = null;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   LOAD MODULE\r\n--------------------------- */\r\n$content = \"\";\r\n\r\nif ($module && file_exists($module)) {\r\n\r\n    ob_start();\r\n    include $module;\r\n    $content = ob_get_clean();\r\n\r\n} else {\r\n\r\n    $content = \"<p style=\'color:red;\'>Module not found.</p>\";\r\n\r\n}\r\n?>\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n<title><?= htmlspecialchars($pageTitle) ?></title>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\nbody {\r\n    margin:0;\r\n    background:#050509;\r\n    color:#f9f9ff;\r\n    font-family:Arial;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.header {\r\n    display:flex;\r\n    justify-content:space-between;\r\n    padding:16px 24px;\r\n    border-bottom:1px solid rgba(245,199,106,0.2);\r\n}\r\n\r\n.nav a {\r\n    margin-left:16px;\r\n    color:#f5c76a;\r\n    text-decoration:none;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.nav a.active {\r\n    border-bottom:1px solid #f5c76a;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.hero-header {\r\n    padding:24px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.hero-content {\r\n    padding:24px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.card-grid {\r\n    display:grid;\r\n    grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);\r\n    gap:16px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.service-card {\r\n    background:#0b0b12;\r\n    padding:16px;\r\n    border-radius:10px;\r\n    border:1px solid rgba(245,199,106,0.2);\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n</head>\r\n\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"header\">\r\n    <div><strong>LEGAiSEE</strong></div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"nav\">\r\n        <a href=\"index.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'index.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Dashboard</a>\r\n        <a href=\"search.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'search.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Search</a>\r\n        <a href=\"ingest.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'ingest.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Ingest</a>\r\n        <a href=\"files.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'files.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Files</a>\r\n\r\n        <span style=\"margin-left:20px;\">|</span>\r\n\r\n        <a href=\"graph.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'graph.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Intelligence</a>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hero-header\">\r\n    <h1><?= htmlspecialchars($pageTitle) ?></h1>\r\n    <p><?= htmlspecialchars($pageDesc) ?></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hero-content\">\r\n    <?= $content ?>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n🧠 WHY THIS FIX WORKS\r\nWe just eliminated:\r\n\r\n$contentFile ambiguity ❌\r\n\r\nvariable overwrite risk ❌\r\n\r\nhidden includes ❌\r\n\r\nlegacy conflicts ❌\r\n\r\nNow:\r\n\r\nURL → module mapping is absolute and deterministic\r\n\r\n🧪 TEST AGAIN\r\n/files.php\r\n→ should show:\r\n🔴 FILES MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\n/graph.php\r\n→ should show:\r\n🟢 GRAPH MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\n🚨 AFTER CONFIRMED\r\nRemove debug lines from both modules.\r\n\r\n🧠 IMPORTANT NOTE\r\nThis is actually more stable for your long-term system because:\r\n\r\nrouting is explicit\r\n\r\nno accidental cross-wiring\r\n\r\neasier to expand (AI modules later)\r\n\r\n👉 NEXT STEP\r\nOnce confirmed:\r\n\r\n“routing 100% fixed”\r\n\r\nWe move into:\r\n\r\n🔥 REAL graph system (node connections, relationships, clustering)\r\n\r\nThis is where your platform becomes actual intelligence infrastructure.\r\n\r\n\r\nFILES MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\nGood. That confirms:\r\n\r\n✅ Routing is now correct\r\n❌ Architecture is now wrong (we broke your intended system to force stability)\r\n\r\nWe’re not leaving it like this.\r\n\r\nRight now you have a hardcoded router in shell.php, but your system is designed to be:\r\n\r\npage → sets $contentFile → shell renders it\r\n\r\nWe’re going to restore that proper architecture, but keep it stable.\r\n\r\n🧠 WHAT ACTUALLY CAUSED THE BUG\r\nEarlier, shell.php was:\r\n\r\neither overwriting $contentFile\r\n\r\nor including a fixed module somewhere\r\n\r\nSo we brute-forced routing to isolate the issue.\r\n\r\nNow that routing works, we revert to the correct design — cleanly.\r\n\r\n🧱 FINAL FIX — RESTORE PROPER ARCHITECTURE (STABLE VERSION)\r\n📁 OPEN:\r\n/commandcenter/shell.php\r\n✂️ DELETE EVERYTHING\r\n✅ REPLACE WITH THIS (FINAL, CORRECT VERSION)\r\n<?php\r\nrequire_once __DIR__ . \"/bootstrap.php\";\r\n\r\n$pageTitle = $pageTitle ?? \"LEGAiSEE\";\r\n$pageDesc  = $pageDesc ?? \"\";\r\n\r\n$current = basename($_SERVER[\'PHP_SELF\']);\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   VALIDATE MODULE INPUT\r\n--------------------------- */\r\n$content = \"\";\r\n\r\nif (\r\n    isset($contentFile) &&\r\n    is_string($contentFile) &&\r\n    file_exists($contentFile)\r\n) {\r\n\r\n    ob_start();\r\n    include $contentFile;\r\n    $content = ob_get_clean();\r\n\r\n} else {\r\n\r\n    $content = \"<p style=\'color:red;\'>Invalid or missing module.</p>\";\r\n\r\n}\r\n?>\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n<title><?= htmlspecialchars($pageTitle) ?></title>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\nbody {\r\n    margin:0;\r\n    background:#050509;\r\n    color:#f9f9ff;\r\n    font-family:Arial;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.header {\r\n    display:flex;\r\n    justify-content:space-between;\r\n    padding:16px 24px;\r\n    border-bottom:1px solid rgba(245,199,106,0.2);\r\n}\r\n\r\n.nav a {\r\n    margin-left:16px;\r\n    color:#f5c76a;\r\n    text-decoration:none;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.nav a.active {\r\n    border-bottom:1px solid #f5c76a;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.hero-header {\r\n    padding:24px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.hero-content {\r\n    padding:24px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.card-grid {\r\n    display:grid;\r\n    grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);\r\n    gap:16px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.service-card {\r\n    background:#0b0b12;\r\n    padding:16px;\r\n    border-radius:10px;\r\n    border:1px solid rgba(245,199,106,0.2);\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n</head>\r\n\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"header\">\r\n    <div><strong>LEGAiSEE</strong></div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"nav\">\r\n        <a href=\"index.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'index.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Dashboard</a>\r\n        <a href=\"search.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'search.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Search</a>\r\n        <a href=\"ingest.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'ingest.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Ingest</a>\r\n        <a href=\"files.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'files.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Files</a>\r\n\r\n        <span style=\"margin-left:20px;\">|</span>\r\n\r\n        <a href=\"graph.php\" class=\"<?= ($current==\'graph.php\')?\'active\':\'\'; ?>\">Intelligence</a>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hero-header\">\r\n    <h1><?= htmlspecialchars($pageTitle) ?></h1>\r\n    <p><?= htmlspecialchars($pageDesc) ?></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hero-content\">\r\n    <?= $content ?>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n🧠 WHY THIS VERSION IS “FINAL”\r\nThis gives you:\r\n\r\n✔ Proper architecture restored\r\npages control modules again\r\n\r\n✔ Safety added\r\nvalidates $contentFile\r\n\r\nprevents silent failure\r\n\r\n✔ No hidden overrides\r\nno hardcoded routing\r\n\r\nno accidental module swaps\r\n\r\n✔ Future-proof\r\nsupports AI modules\r\n\r\nsupports dynamic module injection later\r\n\r\n🧪 FINAL TEST\r\n/files.php\r\n→ should show:\r\nFILES MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\n/graph.php\r\n→ should show:\r\nGRAPH MODULE LOADED\r\n\r\n🚨 AFTER CONFIRMED\r\nRemove your debug lines:\r\n\r\necho \"FILES MODULE LOADED\";\r\necho \"GRAPH MODULE LOADED\";\r\n🧭 SYSTEM STATUS AFTER THIS\r\nYou now have:\r\n\r\n✔ clean rendering engine\r\n✔ correct routing\r\n✔ stable module system\r\n✔ no legacy contamination\r\n✔ architecture aligned with your original design\r\n\r\n🚀 NOW — WE CAN FINALLY MOVE FORWARD\r\nYou are out of “debug hell.”\r\n\r\nNext phase is actual capability:\r\n\r\n🔥 REAL graph system\r\n(node relationships, clustering, intelligence mapping)\r\n\r\n👉 NEXT STEP\r\nSay:\r\n\r\n“build real graph system”\r\n\r\nAnd we move into the part that actually creates value for your business model.\r\n\r\n\r\nconfirmed\r\n\r\nGood. System is now stable, correctly routed, and architecturally clean.\r\n\r\nWe move forward — no more fixes, only capability.\r\n\r\n🧠 PHASE: REAL GRAPH SYSTEM (NODE RELATIONSHIPS)\r\nRight now your “graph” is just a list.\r\n\r\nWe are turning it into:\r\n\r\na true relationship engine + visual node map\r\n\r\n🧱 WHAT WE ARE BUILDING (FULL SCOPE)\r\n1. Relationship Table (edges)\r\n2. Save relationships between nodes\r\n3. Graph data API (JSON endpoint)\r\n4. Interactive visualization (force-directed graph)\r\n5. Click → open node (view.php)\r\n🧱 STEP 1 — DATABASE (RELATIONSHIPS)\r\n📍 GO TO: phpMyAdmin → SQL tab\r\n▶️ RUN THIS:\r\nCREATE TABLE page_relations (\r\n    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    source_id INT NOT NULL,\r\n    target_id INT NOT NULL,\r\n    relation_type VARCHAR(100) DEFAULT \'related\',\r\n    weight FLOAT DEFAULT 1,\r\n    created TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\r\n\r\n    INDEX (source_id),\r\n    INDEX (target_id)\r\n);\r\n🧠 WHAT THIS DOES\r\nYou now have:\r\n\r\npage A → page B\r\nThis is the foundation of:\r\n\r\nclustering\r\n\r\nAI linking\r\n\r\ntopic grouping\r\n\r\nbusiness archaeology chains\r\n\r\n🧱 STEP 2 — GRAPH DATA API\r\nWe need raw data for visualization.\r\n\r\n📁 CREATE NEW FILE:\r\n/commandcenter/graph_data.php\r\n🔁 FULL FILE:\r\n<?php\r\nrequire_once __DIR__ . \"/bootstrap.php\";\r\n\r\nheader(\'Content-Type: application/json\');\r\n\r\n/* NODES */\r\n$nodesStmt = $pdo->query(\"\r\n    SELECT id, title\r\n    FROM page\r\n    ORDER BY created DESC\r\n    LIMIT 200\r\n\");\r\n\r\n$nodes = [];\r\n\r\nforeach ($nodesStmt as $row) {\r\n    $nodes[] = [\r\n        \"id\" => (int)$row[\'id\'],\r\n        \"label\" => $row[\'title\']\r\n    ];\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* LINKS */\r\n$linksStmt = $pdo->query(\"\r\n    SELECT source_id, target_id, weight\r\n    FROM page_relations\r\n    LIMIT 500\r\n\");\r\n\r\n$links = [];\r\n\r\nforeach ($linksStmt as $row) {\r\n    $links[] = [\r\n        \"source\" => (int)$row[\'source_id\'],\r\n        \"target\" => (int)$row[\'target_id\'],\r\n        \"value\"  => (float)$row[\'weight\']\r\n    ];\r\n}\r\n\r\necho json_encode([\r\n    \"nodes\" => $nodes,\r\n    \"links\" => $links\r\n]);\r\n🧱 STEP 3 — REAL GRAPH UI\r\nWe replace your fake graph cards with a real visualization.\r\n\r\n📁 OPEN:\r\n/commandcenter/modules/graph_module.php\r\n✂️ DELETE EVERYTHING\r\n✅ REPLACE WITH:\r\n<?php\r\n?>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"graph\" style=\"height:600px;\"></div>\r\n\r\n<script src=\"https://d3js.org/d3.v7.min.js\"></script>\r\n\r\n<script>\r\n\r\nfetch(\'graph_data.php\')\r\n.then(res => res.json())\r\n.then(data => {\r\n\r\n    const width = document.getElementById(\'graph\').clientWidth;\r\n    const height = 600;\r\n\r\n    const svg = d3.select(\"#graph\")\r\n        .append(\"svg\")\r\n        .attr(\"width\", width)\r\n        .attr(\"height\", height);\r\n\r\n    const simulation = d3.forceSimulation(data.nodes)\r\n        .force(\"link\", d3.forceLink(data.links).id(d => d.id).distance(120))\r\n        .force(\"charge\", d3.forceManyBody().strength(-300))\r\n        .force(\"center\", d3.forceCenter(width / 2, height / 2));\r\n\r\n    const link = svg.append(\"g\")\r\n        .selectAll(\"line\")\r\n        .data(data.links)\r\n        .enter()\r\n        .append(\"line\")\r\n        .style(\"stroke\", \"#999\");\r\n\r\n    const node = svg.append(\"g\")\r\n        .selectAll(\"circle\")\r\n        .data(data.nodes)\r\n        .enter()\r\n        .append(\"circle\")\r\n        .attr(\"r\", 6)\r\n        .style(\"fill\", \"#f5c76a\")\r\n        .call(d3.drag()\r\n            .on(\"start\", dragstart)\r\n            .on(\"drag\", drag)\r\n            .on(\"end\", dragend)\r\n        )\r\n        .on(\"click\", (event, d) => {\r\n            window.location = \"view.php?id=\" + d.id;\r\n        });\r\n\r\n    const label = svg.append(\"g\")\r\n        .selectAll(\"text\")\r\n        .data(data.nodes)\r\n        .enter()\r\n        .append(\"text\")\r\n        .text(d => d.label)\r\n        .style(\"font-size\", \"10px\")\r\n        .style(\"fill\", \"#fff\");\r\n\r\n    simulation.on(\"tick\", () => {\r\n\r\n        link\r\n            .attr(\"x1\", d => d.source.x)\r\n            .attr(\"y1\", d => d.source.y)\r\n            .attr(\"x2\", d => d.target.x)\r\n            .attr(\"y2\", d => d.target.y);\r\n\r\n        node\r\n            .attr(\"cx\", d => d.x)\r\n            .attr(\"cy\", d => d.y);\r\n\r\n        label\r\n            .attr(\"x\", d => d.x + 8)\r\n            .attr(\"y\", d => d.y + 3);\r\n\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    function dragstart(event, d) {\r\n        if (!event.active) simulation.alphaTarget(0.3).restart();\r\n        d.fx = d.x;\r\n        d.fy = d.y;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    function drag(event, d) {\r\n        d.fx = event.x;\r\n        d.fy = event.y;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    function dragend(event, d) {\r\n        if (!event.active) simulation.alphaTarget(0);\r\n        d.fx = null;\r\n        d.fy = null;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n});\r\n</script>\r\n🧠 WHAT YOU NOW HAVE\r\n✔ REAL graph visualization\r\n✔ nodes = pages\r\n✔ edges = relationships\r\n✔ drag interaction\r\n✔ click → open record\r\n✔ scalable foundation\r\n🚨 IMPORTANT (RIGHT NOW)\r\nGraph will appear:\r\n\r\nnodes floating\r\n\r\nmaybe no connections yet\r\n\r\nThat’s normal.\r\n\r\nBecause:\r\n\r\nyou haven’t created relationships yet\r\n\r\n🚀 NEXT STEP (CRITICAL)\r\nWe now build:\r\n\r\n🔗 RELATIONSHIP CREATION SYSTEM\r\n\r\nSo ingest/search can:\r\n\r\nlink nodes\r\n\r\nauto-suggest relationships\r\n\r\nbuild clusters\r\n\r\n👉 NEXT COMMAND\r\nSay:\r\n\r\n“build relationship system”\r\n\r\nThat’s where this becomes:\r\n\r\n🔥 Business Archaeology Engine\r\n—not just visualization.\r\n\r\n\r\nbuild relationship system\r\n\r\nGood. This is where the system actually becomes intelligence infrastructure instead of storage.\r\n\r\nWe’re building a complete relationship system in one pass — no fragments.\r\n\r\n🧠 WHAT YOU WILL HAVE AFTER THIS\r\n✔ Manually link any node → any node\r\n✔ Store relationship type + weight\r\n✔ View relationships on a record\r\n✔ Navigate between connected nodes\r\n✔ Feed graph visualization with real data\r\n\r\n🧱 STEP 1 — VERIFY DATABASE (ALREADY CREATED)\r\nYou should already have:\r\n\r\npage_relations (\r\n  id\r\n  source_id\r\n  target_id\r\n  relation_type\r\n  weight\r\n  created\r\n)\r\nIf not, stop and create it.\r\n\r\n🧱 STEP 2 — RELATIONSHIP CREATION (UI + SAVE)\r\nWe will embed this directly into view.php flow (correct place).\r\n\r\n📁 CREATE NEW FILE:\r\n/commandcenter/modules/relations_module.php\r\n🔁 FULL FILE:\r\n<?php\r\n\r\n$currentId = $_GET[\'id\'] ?? 0;\r\n\r\n/* SAVE RELATION */\r\nif ($_SERVER[\'REQUEST_METHOD\'] === \'POST\' && isset($_POST[\'target_id\'])) {\r\n\r\n    $stmt = $pdo->prepare(\"\r\n        INSERT INTO page_relations (source_id, target_id, relation_type, weight)\r\n        VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\r\n    \");\r\n\r\n    $stmt->execute([\r\n        $currentId,\r\n        $_POST[\'target_id\'],\r\n        $_POST[\'relation_type\'] ?? \'related\',\r\n        $_POST[\'weight\'] ?? 1\r\n    ]);\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* LOAD ALL OTHER NODES */\r\n$nodes = $pdo->prepare(\"\r\n    SELECT id, title\r\n    FROM page\r\n    WHERE id != ?\r\n    ORDER BY created DESC\r\n    LIMIT 200\r\n\");\r\n\r\n$nodes->execute([$currentId]);\r\n\r\n/* LOAD EXISTING RELATIONS */\r\n$relations = $pdo->prepare(\"\r\n    SELECT pr.*, p.title as target_title\r\n    FROM page_relations pr\r\n    JOIN page p ON p.id = pr.target_id\r\n    WHERE pr.source_id = ?\r\n\");\r\n\r\n$relations->execute([$currentId]);\r\n\r\n?>\r\n\r\n<h2>Relationships</h2>\r\n\r\n<form method=\"POST\">\r\n\r\n    <select name=\"target_id\">\r\n        <?php foreach ($nodes as $n): ?>\r\n            <option value=\"<?= $n[\'id\'] ?>\">\r\n                <?= htmlspecialchars($n[\'title\']) ?>\r\n            </option>\r\n        <?php endforeach; ?>\r\n    </select>\r\n\r\n    <input name=\"relation_type\" placeholder=\"Relation type (e.g. derived, similar, campaign)\">\r\n\r\n    <input name=\"weight\" placeholder=\"Weight (1-10)\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\">\r\n\r\n    <button class=\"btn btn-primary\">Add Relationship</button>\r\n\r\n</form>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-grid\">\r\n\r\n<?php foreach ($relations as $r): ?>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"service-card\">\r\n        <h3><?= htmlspecialchars($r[\'target_title\']) ?></h3>\r\n        <p>Type: <?= htmlspecialchars($r[\'relation_type\']) ?></p>\r\n        <p>Weight: <?= $r[\'weight\'] ?></p>\r\n        <a href=\"view.php?id=<?= $r[\'target_id\'] ?>\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Open</a>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n<?php endforeach; ?>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n🧱 STEP 3 — INJECT INTO RECORD VIEW\r\nWe now attach relationships to every record.\r\n\r\n📁 OPEN:\r\n/commandcenter/modules/view_module.php\r\n✂️ DELETE EVERYTHING\r\n✅ REPLACE WITH:\r\n<?php\r\n\r\n$id = $_GET[\'id\'] ?? 0;\r\n\r\n/* LOAD PAGE */\r\n$stmt = $pdo->prepare(\"SELECT * FROM page WHERE id = ?\");\r\n$stmt->execute([$id]);\r\n$page = $stmt->fetch();\r\n\r\n/* LOAD CONTENT */\r\n$stmt2 = $pdo->prepare(\"SELECT content FROM page_content WHERE page_id = ?\");\r\n$stmt2->execute([$id]);\r\n$contentRow = $stmt2->fetch();\r\n\r\n?>\r\n\r\n<?php if (!$page): ?>\r\n    <p>Record not found.</p>\r\n<?php else: ?>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"service-card\">\r\n    <h2><?= htmlspecialchars($page[\'title\']) ?></h2>\r\n    <p><?= $page[\'project\'] ?> | <?= $page[\'platform\'] ?> | <?= $page[\'type\'] ?></p>\r\n    <hr>\r\n    <div><?= nl2br(htmlspecialchars($contentRow[\'content\'] ?? \'\')) ?></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<?php include __DIR__ . \"/relations_module.php\"; ?>\r\n\r\n<?php endif; ?>\r\n🧠 WHAT THIS DOES\r\nEvery record now has:\r\n\r\n✔ full content display\r\n✔ relationship builder\r\n✔ relationship list\r\n✔ navigation between nodes\r\n🧱 STEP 4 — OPTIONAL (BUT STRONG UPGRADE)\r\nMake relationships bi-directional visible\r\n\r\nUPDATE relations query inside relations_module.php\r\nReplace:\r\n\r\nWHERE pr.source_id = ?\r\nWITH:\r\n\r\nWHERE pr.source_id = ? OR pr.target_id = ?\r\nAND update execute:\r\n\r\n$relations->execute([$currentId, $currentId]);\r\n🧠 RESULT\r\nNow you see:\r\n\r\noutgoing relationships\r\n\r\nincoming relationships\r\n\r\nThis is critical for true graph intelligence\r\n\r\n🧪 TEST FLOW\r\nGo to any record:\r\n\r\n/view.php?id=1\r\nAdd relationship\r\n\r\nRefresh\r\n\r\nClick linked node\r\n\r\nYou now have a chain\r\n\r\n🚀 YOU NOW HAVE\r\n✔ relational database layer\r\n✔ UI for linking nodes\r\n✔ navigation across relationships\r\n✔ data feeding graph visualization\r\n🧠 THIS IS THE TURNING POINT\r\nYou now moved from:\r\n\r\n“CMS”\r\n\r\nto:\r\n\r\ngraph-based intelligence system\r\n\r\n🚀 NEXT PHASE (HIGH VALUE)\r\nNow we add automation:\r\n\r\n🔥 Auto-link suggestions\r\nbased on title similarity\r\n\r\nbased on tags\r\n\r\nbased on content similarity\r\n\r\n🔥 Clustering engine\r\ngroup nodes into topics\r\n\r\n🔥 AI extraction layer\r\ndetect relationships automatically\r\n\r\n👉 NEXT STEP\r\nSay:\r\n\r\n“build auto-linking system”\r\n\r\nThat’s where this becomes real Business Archaeology intelligence, not manual linking.\r\n\r\n\r\nrelations=Warning: Undefined variable $pdo in /home/carrmulti/www/www/commandcenter/modules/relations_module.php on line 22\r\n\r\nFatal error: Uncaught Error: Call to a member function prepare() on null in /home/carrmulti/www/www/commandcenter/modules/relations_module.php:22 Stack trace: #0 {main} thrown in /home/carrmulti/www/www/commandcenter/modules/relations_module.php on line 22\r\n\r\nGood — this is a clean, isolated issue.\r\n\r\n❌ $pdo is NOT available inside relations_module.php\r\n\r\nThat means:\r\n\r\nbootstrap.php is NOT being loaded into that module’s scope\r\n\r\n🧠 ROOT CAUSE\r\nYour system flow is:\r\n\r\npage.php → shell.php → module\r\nBUT:\r\n\r\n👉 relations_module.php is being included inside another module (view_module.php)\r\n\r\nSo it does NOT automatically inherit $pdo unless we explicitly make sure it’s available.\r\n\r\n🧱 FIX — GUARANTEE PDO IN MODULE (SAFE + PERMANENT)\r\nWe will safely inject $pdo if missing.\r\n\r\n📁 OPEN:\r\n/commandcenter/modules/relations_module.php\r\n✂️ DELETE EVERYTHING\r\n✅ REPLACE WITH THIS FULL FILE:\r\n<?php\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   ENSURE DATABASE ACCESS\r\n--------------------------- */\r\nif (!isset($pdo)) {\r\n    require_once __DIR__ . \"/../bootstrap.php\";\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   GET CURRENT ID\r\n--------------------------- */\r\n$currentId = $_GET[\'id\'] ?? 0;\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   SAVE RELATION\r\n--------------------------- */\r\nif ($_SERVER[\'REQUEST_METHOD\'] === \'POST\' && isset($_POST[\'target_id\'])) {\r\n\r\n    $stmt = $pdo->prepare(\"\r\n        INSERT INTO page_relations (source_id, target_id, relation_type, weight)\r\n        VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\r\n    \");\r\n\r\n    $stmt->execute([\r\n        $currentId,\r\n        $_POST[\'target_id\'],\r\n        $_POST[\'relation_type\'] ?? \'related\',\r\n        $_POST[\'weight\'] ?? 1\r\n    ]);\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   LOAD OTHER NODES\r\n--------------------------- */\r\n$nodes = $pdo->prepare(\"\r\n    SELECT id, title\r\n    FROM page\r\n    WHERE id != ?\r\n    ORDER BY created DESC\r\n    LIMIT 200\r\n\");\r\n\r\n$nodes->execute([$currentId]);\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   LOAD RELATIONSHIPS (BI-DIRECTIONAL)\r\n--------------------------- */\r\n$relations = $pdo->prepare(\"\r\n    SELECT pr.*, p.title as target_title\r\n    FROM page_relations pr\r\n    JOIN page p \r\n        ON p.id = IF(pr.source_id = ?, pr.target_id, pr.source_id)\r\n    WHERE pr.source_id = ? OR pr.target_id = ?\r\n\");\r\n\r\n$relations->execute([$currentId, $currentId, $currentId]);\r\n\r\n?>\r\n\r\n<h2>Relationships</h2>\r\n\r\n<form method=\"POST\">\r\n\r\n    <select name=\"target_id\">\r\n        <?php foreach ($nodes as $n): ?>\r\n            <option value=\"<?= $n[\'id\'] ?>\">\r\n                <?= htmlspecialchars($n[\'title\']) ?>\r\n            </option>\r\n        <?php endforeach; ?>\r\n    </select>\r\n\r\n    <input name=\"relation_type\" placeholder=\"Relation type (e.g. derived, similar, campaign)\">\r\n\r\n    <input name=\"weight\" placeholder=\"Weight (1-10)\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\">\r\n\r\n    <button class=\"btn btn-primary\">Add Relationship</button>\r\n\r\n</form>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-grid\">\r\n\r\n<?php foreach ($relations as $r): ?>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"service-card\">\r\n        <h3><?= htmlspecialchars($r[\'target_title\']) ?></h3>\r\n        <p>Type: <?= htmlspecialchars($r[\'relation_type\']) ?></p>\r\n        <p>Weight: <?= $r[\'weight\'] ?></p>\r\n        <a href=\"view.php?id=<?= ($r[\'source_id\'] == $currentId ? $r[\'target_id\'] : $r[\'source_id\']) ?>\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">\r\n            Open\r\n        </a>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n<?php endforeach; ?>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n🧠 WHY THIS FIX WORKS\r\n✔ Guarantees $pdo exists\r\nif (!isset($pdo)) require bootstrap\r\n✔ Works regardless of nesting\r\ndirect include ✔\r\n\r\nnested include ✔\r\n\r\nfuture modules ✔\r\n\r\n✔ Fixes bidirectional relationship logic cleanly\r\n🧪 TEST\r\nGo to:\r\n\r\n/view.php?id=1\r\nYou should now see:\r\n\r\ndropdown of nodes\r\n\r\nadd relationship button\r\n\r\nrelationship cards below\r\n\r\n🚨 IMPORTANT SYSTEM RULE (LOCK THIS)\r\nFor ALL future modules:\r\n\r\nIf module uses DB → always ensure $pdo exists\r\n\r\nPattern:\r\n\r\nif (!isset($pdo)) {\r\n    require_once __DIR__ . \"/../bootstrap.php\";\r\n}\r\n🚀 NEXT STEP\r\nNow that relationships work:\r\n\r\nSay:\r\n\r\n“build auto-linking system”\r\n\r\nThat’s where this becomes:\r\n\r\n🔥 AI-assisted intelligence engine (not manual work)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', '2026-04-22 23:34:12');
INSERT INTO `page_content` (`id`, `page_id`, `content`, `created`) VALUES
(2, 2, '\r\n\r\n🧠 LEGAiSEE SYSTEM — MEMORY DUMP (NEW CHAT HANDOFF)\r\n📌 SYSTEM IDENTITY\r\n\r\nYou are working on a PHP + MySQL web system called:\r\n\r\nLEGAiSEE Command Center\r\n\r\nIt is a lightweight internal intelligence/CMS system designed for:\r\n\r\nstoring structured “pages”\r\ningesting content\r\nsearching records\r\nviewing individual entries\r\n🧱 CURRENT ARCHITECTURE (FINALIZED)\r\nDATABASE (MySQL — ACTIVE)\r\nTABLE 1: page\r\n\r\nStores metadata + tags\r\n\r\nid (int, PK)\r\ntitle (text)\r\nproject (text)\r\nplatform (text)\r\ntype (text)\r\ncreated (timestamp)\r\nTABLE 2: page_content\r\n\r\nStores full content\r\n\r\nid (int, PK)\r\npage_id (int, FK → page.id)\r\ncontent (longtext)\r\ncreated (timestamp)\r\n🔗 DATA RELATIONSHIP MODEL\r\npage (metadata)\r\n   ↓ 1-to-1\r\npage_content (body)\r\n🧠 CORE SYSTEM BEHAVIOR\r\n1. INGEST\r\nCreates a page\r\nImmediately creates matching page_content\r\nLinks via page_id\r\n2. SEARCH\r\nSearches:\r\npage.title\r\npage_content.content\r\nReturns page results (not raw content)\r\nDisplays tags:\r\nproject\r\nplatform\r\ntype\r\n3. VIEW\r\nLoads page by id\r\nLoads matching page_content by page_id\r\nDisplays combined record\r\n🎨 UI SYSTEM (LOCKED DESIGN)\r\nLayout Rules\r\ndark theme\r\ngold accent (#f5c76a)\r\ncard-based system\r\ngrid dashboard layout\r\nComponents\r\n.service-card = primary UI block\r\n.card-grid = 3-column layout (responsive)\r\n.btn btn-primary = gradient gold button\r\n🧭 NAVIGATION SYSTEM\r\n\r\nPersistent top nav on all pages:\r\n\r\nDashboard (index.php)\r\nSearch (search.php)\r\nIngest (ingest.php)\r\nFiles (files.php)\r\n🧠 CURRENT FEATURES STATUS\r\nCOMPLETE\r\npage + page_content database structure\r\ningest system (working)\r\nsearch system (working)\r\nview system (working)\r\nUI shell (grid + cards + nav)\r\nIN PROGRESS / NEXT PHASE\r\nfilter system (by project/platform/type)\r\nfile/archive refinement\r\nAI summarization layer\r\ntagging-based intelligence queries\r\n⚠️ IMPORTANT RULES FOR FUTURE DEVELOPMENT\r\nNEVER reference records table (does not exist)\r\nALWAYS use page + page_content\r\npage must always be created BEFORE page_content\r\npage_content must always reference page_id\r\ntags are stored ONLY in page\r\ncontent is stored ONLY in page_content\r\n🧱 SYSTEM FLOW (FINAL TRUTH)\r\nINGEST → page → page_content\r\nSEARCH → page + page_content\r\nVIEW → page + page_content\r\n🚀 CURRENT OBJECTIVE STATE\r\n\r\nSystem is now:\r\n\r\nstable CMS core with tagging-ready architecture\r\n\r\nNext evolution is:\r\n\r\nFILTER + INTELLIGENCE LAYER\r\n\r\n(not UI fixes, not database fixes)\r\n\r\n📌 START OF NEW CHAT INSTRUCTION PROMPT\r\n\r\nPaste this into a new chat:\r\n\r\n🔥 START PROMPT\r\n\r\nYou are continuing work on a PHP/MySQL system called LEGAiSEE Command Center.\r\n\r\nThe system is already built with:\r\n\r\ntable page (id, title, project, platform, type, created)\r\ntable page_content (id, page_id, content, created)\r\n\r\nArchitecture rules:\r\n\r\npage stores metadata + tags\r\npage_content stores body text\r\npage must always be created first\r\npage_content links via page_id\r\n\r\nCore modules already exist and are working:\r\n\r\ningest (creates page + page_content)\r\nsearch (queries page + page_content)\r\nview (renders combined record)\r\n\r\nUI system:\r\n\r\ndark theme\r\ngold accent\r\ncard-based grid layout\r\npersistent navigation\r\n\r\nDO NOT:\r\n\r\nintroduce new tables\r\nrevert to “records” model\r\nchange architecture unless explicitly requested\r\n\r\nNext development phase will be:\r\nfiltering system (project/platform/type)\r\n\r\nContinue from this stable state.\r\n\r\n🧠 END RESULT\r\n\r\nThis gives you:\r\n\r\nclean reset point\r\nno chat drift\r\nno schema confusion\r\ndeterministic continuation\r\n\r\nUnderstood. I’ve absorbed this as the canonical system state for LEGAiSEE Command Center.\r\n\r\nHere is your clean continuation baseline (validated + normalized for future development) so the next chat starts with zero ambiguity:\r\n\r\n🧠 LEGAiSEE COMMAND CENTER — STABLE SYSTEM STATE (v1.0)\r\n🧱 DATABASE ARCHITECTURE (LOCKED)\r\nTABLE: page (METADATA ONLY)\r\nStores all searchable and filterable attributes.\r\n\r\nid (int, PK)\r\n\r\ntitle (text)\r\n\r\nproject (text)\r\n\r\nplatform (text)\r\n\r\ntype (text)\r\n\r\ncreated (timestamp)\r\n\r\nTABLE: page_content (BODY ONLY)\r\nStores full content payload.\r\n\r\nid (int, PK)\r\n\r\npage_id (int, FK → page.id)\r\n\r\ncontent (longtext)\r\n\r\ncreated (timestamp)\r\n\r\n🔗 RELATIONSHIP MODEL\r\npage (metadata + tags)\r\n   ↓ 1-to-1\r\npage_content (full content body)\r\n🧠 CORE SYSTEM BEHAVIOR (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\r\n1. INGEST FLOW\r\nCreate page FIRST\r\n\r\nImmediately create page_content\r\n\r\nLink via page_id\r\n\r\n2. SEARCH FLOW\r\nSearch across:\r\n\r\npage.title\r\n\r\npage_content.content\r\n\r\nReturn:\r\n\r\npage results only (NOT raw content)\r\n\r\ninclude metadata tags:\r\n\r\nproject\r\n\r\nplatform\r\n\r\ntype\r\n\r\n3. VIEW FLOW\r\nLoad page by id\r\n\r\nLoad page_content by page_id\r\n\r\nMerge for display\r\n\r\n🎨 UI SYSTEM (LOCKED DESIGN LANGUAGE)\r\nVisual Style\r\nDark theme\r\n\r\nGold accent: #f5c76a\r\n\r\nCard-based UI\r\n\r\nGrid layout\r\n\r\nComponents\r\n.service-card → primary content block\r\n\r\n.card-grid → responsive 3-column system\r\n\r\n.btn.btn-primary → gold gradient CTA\r\n\r\n🧭 NAVIGATION (GLOBAL PERSISTENT)\r\nDashboard → index.php\r\n\r\nSearch → search.php\r\n\r\nIngest → ingest.php\r\n\r\nFiles → files.php\r\n\r\n⚠️ HARD CONSTRAINTS (DO NOT BREAK)\r\n❌ Never use records table\r\n❌ Never introduce new tables\r\n❌ Never store content inside page\r\n❌ Never store tags inside page_content\r\n❌ Never create page_content before page\r\n\r\n🧠 SYSTEM FLOW (TRUTH MODEL)\r\nINGEST → page → page_content\r\nSEARCH → page + page_content\r\nVIEW → page + page_content\r\n🚀 CURRENT STATE CLASSIFICATION\r\nSystem status:\r\n\r\n✔ Stable CMS Core\r\n✔ Metadata + Content Separation Complete\r\n✔ Search + View + Ingest Operational\r\n✔ UI Framework Established\r\n✔ Ready for Intelligence Layer Expansion\r\n\r\n🧭 NEXT PHASE (ONLY VALID ROADMAP STEP)\r\nFILTER + INTELLIGENCE LAYER\r\nUpcoming capabilities:\r\n\r\nfilter by project\r\n\r\nfilter by platform\r\n\r\nfilter by type\r\n\r\ncombined query logic (AND/OR grouping later phase)\r\n\r\n📌 READY STATE CONFIRMATION\r\nThis is now a deterministic rebuild anchor.\r\n\r\nAny new chat starting from this state should assume:\r\n\r\n“The CMS core is complete. We are building intelligence filtering on top of it.”\r\n\r\nIf you want next step precision, I can design:\r\n\r\nSQL filter queries (safe + scalable)\r\n\r\nPHP filter engine (drop-in code)\r\n\r\nUI filter panel (grid-native, gold UI consistent)\r\n\r\nOR full “intelligence layer architecture” before coding\r\n\r\nJust tell me the direction.\r\n\r\n\r\nSQL filter queries (safe + scalable)\r\n\r\nBelow is a clean, production-safe SQL filter layer for your LEGAiSEE schema that stays consistent with your architecture rules and scales without restructuring tables.\r\n\r\nWe’ll design this as a single-query flexible filter system built on page + optional join to page_content.\r\n\r\n🧠 LEGAiSEE — FILTER QUERY LAYER (SQL)\r\n🧱 BASE PRINCIPLE\r\nAll filtering happens on:\r\n\r\npage (primary filter source)\r\n\r\noptional JOIN page_content (only for search)\r\n\r\nNo schema changes. No extra tables.\r\n\r\n🔍 1. BASE SEARCH + FILTER QUERY (CORE PATTERN)\r\nSELECT \r\n    p.id,\r\n    p.title,\r\n    p.project,\r\n    p.platform,\r\n    p.type,\r\n    p.created\r\nFROM page p\r\nLEFT JOIN page_content pc ON pc.page_id = p.id\r\nWHERE 1=1\r\nThis WHERE 1=1 is intentional:\r\n→ makes dynamic filtering safe and composable in PHP\r\n\r\n🎯 2. FILTER BY INDIVIDUAL FIELDS\r\n📁 Project Filter\r\nAND p.project = ?\r\n🧩 Platform Filter\r\nAND p.platform = ?\r\n🏷 Type Filter\r\nAND p.type = ?\r\n🔎 3. FULL-TEXT SEARCH (SAFE OPTION)\r\nBecause MySQL fulltext may or may not be enabled, here are two safe layers:\r\n\r\nOption A (SAFE DEFAULT — LIKE search)\r\nAND (\r\n    p.title LIKE ?\r\n    OR pc.content LIKE ?\r\n)\r\nBind value:\r\n\r\n%keyword%\r\nOption B (ADVANCED — FULLTEXT if enabled)\r\nIf you later enable FULLTEXT indexes:\r\n\r\nAND (\r\n    MATCH(p.title) AGAINST (? IN NATURAL LANGUAGE MODE)\r\n    OR MATCH(pc.content) AGAINST (? IN NATURAL LANGUAGE MODE)\r\n)\r\n⚙️ 4. COMBINED FILTER QUERY (PRODUCTION READY)\r\nThis is your final scalable query template:\r\n\r\nSELECT \r\n    p.id,\r\n    p.title,\r\n    p.project,\r\n    p.platform,\r\n    p.type,\r\n    p.created\r\nFROM page p\r\nLEFT JOIN page_content pc ON pc.page_id = p.id\r\nWHERE 1=1\r\n\r\n-- PROJECT FILTER\r\nAND (? IS NULL OR p.project = ?)\r\n\r\n-- PLATFORM FILTER\r\nAND (? IS NULL OR p.platform = ?)\r\n\r\n-- TYPE FILTER\r\nAND (? IS NULL OR p.type = ?)\r\n\r\n-- SEARCH FILTER\r\nAND (\r\n    ? IS NULL OR p.title LIKE ?\r\n    OR pc.content LIKE ?\r\n)\r\n\r\nORDER BY p.created DESC\r\nLIMIT ? OFFSET ?\r\n🧠 5. WHY THIS PATTERN SCALES\r\n✔ SAFE\r\nNo string concatenation needed\r\n\r\nFully parameterized (PDO-safe)\r\n\r\n✔ FLEXIBLE\r\nAny filter can be NULL (ignored automatically)\r\n\r\n✔ EXTENDABLE\r\nYou can later add:\r\n\r\ndate ranges\r\n\r\ntag expansion layer\r\n\r\nscoring system\r\n\r\nranking weights\r\n\r\n🚀 6. OPTIONAL: PERFORMANCE UPGRADE INDEXES\r\nAdd these for scale:\r\n\r\nCREATE INDEX idx_page_project ON page(project);\r\nCREATE INDEX idx_page_platform ON page(platform);\r\nCREATE INDEX idx_page_type ON page(type);\r\nCREATE INDEX idx_page_created ON page(created);\r\nCREATE INDEX idx_page_content_page_id ON page_content(page_id);\r\n🧭 7. FUTURE INTELLIGENCE LAYER HOOK (IMPORTANT)\r\nThis structure is already prepared for:\r\n\r\nPhase 2 upgrades:\r\nweighted scoring search\r\n\r\nfilter stacking logic (AND/OR groups)\r\n\r\nAI ranking of results\r\n\r\nsemantic search overlay (external or hybrid)\r\n\r\n📌 IF YOU WANT NEXT STEP\r\nI can build the