ame=\"content\" placeholder=\"Content\"></textarea>\r\n\r\n    <button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Save Node</button>\r\n\r\n</form>\r\n🧠 WHAT THIS FIX DOES (IMPORTANT)\r\nNow:\r\n\r\n✔ ingest.php = controller only\r\n✔ shell.php = ONLY renderer\r\n✔ view file = ONLY UI\r\nNO MORE:\r\n\r\n$content conflicts\r\n\r\noverwrites\r\n\r\nhidden wiping\r\n\r\nmixed rendering systems\r\n\r\n🧭 WHY YOU SAW BLANK FORM BEFORE\r\nBecause:\r\n\r\nshell.php overwrote $content after ingest created it\r\n\r\nSo form existed briefly → then got replaced.\r\n\r\n🚀 AFTER THIS WORKS\r\nYou will now have:\r\n\r\n✔ consistent UI everywhere\r\n✔ no disappearing content\r\n✔ clean separation of logic/UI\r\n✔ stable shell rendering system\r\n\r\n👉 NEXT STEP\r\nApply this and tell me:\r\n\r\n“ingest fixed”\r\n\r\nThen we proceed to the real interface phase (graph + search intelligence upgrade) with a stable architecture finally locked.\r\n\r\n\r\nfiles=Fatal error: Uncaught Error: Call to undefined function getDB() in /home/carrmulti/www/www/commandcenter/modules/files_module.php:4 Stack trace: #0 /home/carrmulti/www/www/commandcenter/shell.php(11): include() #1 /home/carrmulti/www/www/commandcenter/files.php(9): include(\'/home/carrmulti...\') #2 {main} thrown in /home/carrmulti/www/www/commandcenter/modules/files_module.php on line 4\r\n\r\nGood — this one is clean and very specific. We’re not dealing with UI anymore. This is a function mismatch in your legacy module layer.\r\n\r\n🧠 ROOT CAUSE\r\nError:\r\n\r\nCall to undefined function getDB()\r\nMeaning:\r\n\r\nYour files_module.php is written for a different database architecture than the one you currently standardized.\r\n\r\nRight now your system uses:\r\n\r\n$pdo\r\nBut files_module.php is trying to use:\r\n\r\ngetDB()\r\nThat function does not exist anywhere in your current stack.\r\n\r\n💥 WHAT THIS REALLY MEANS\r\nYou now have:\r\n\r\nLayer	Status\r\nshell.php system	✔ modern\r\nbootstrap.php + PDO	✔ modern\r\ningest/search/dashboard	✔ modern\r\nfiles_module.php	❌ legacy orphan code\r\n🧱 FIX STRATEGY (NO PATCHING — FULL REPLACEMENT)\r\nWe will convert files_module.php to match your current PDO architecture.\r\n\r\n📁 STEP 1 — REPLACE ENTIRE modules/files_module.php\r\nFULL FIXED VERSION:\r\n<?php\r\n// USE EXISTING SYSTEM CONNECTION\r\nrequire_once __DIR__ . \"/../bootstrap.php\";\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   FETCH FILE-LIKE RECORDS\r\n--------------------------- */\r\n$stmt = $pdo->prepare(\"\r\n    SELECT id, title, project, platform, type, created\r\n    FROM page\r\n    ORDER BY created DESC\r\n    LIMIT 200\r\n\");\r\n\r\n$stmt->execute();\r\n$files = $stmt->fetchAll();\r\n\r\n/* --------------------------\r\n   OUTPUT (USED INSIDE SHELL)\r\n--------------------------- */\r\nob_start();\r\n?>\r\n\r\n<h2>Files</h2>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"grid\">\r\n\r\n<?php foreach ($files as $f): ?>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"card\">\r\n\r\n        <div style=\"color:#f5c76a; font-weight:bold;\">\r\n            <?= htmlspecialchars($f[\'title\']) ?>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div style=\"font-size:12px; opacity:0.7;\">\r\n            <?= $f[\'project\'] ?> | <?= $f[\'platform\'] ?> | <?= $f[\'type\'] ?>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div style=\"font-size:10px; opacity:0.5;\">\r\n            <?= $f[\'created\'] ?>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n<?php endforeach; ?>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<?php\r\n$content = ob_get_clean();\r\n📁 STEP 2 — FIX files.php (CRITICAL)\r\nMake sure files.php is ONLY a shell wrapper:\r\n\r\n<?php\r\nrequire_once __DIR__ . \"/bootstrap.php\";\r\n\r\n$pageTitle = \"Files\";\r\n$pageDesc = \"Intelligence archive view\";\r\n\r\n$contentFile = __DIR__ . \"/modules/files_module.php\";\r\n\r\ninclude __DIR__ . \"/shell.php\";\r\n🧠 WHY THIS BROKE\r\nBecause your system evolved through 3 phases:\r\n\r\n1. Old system\r\nused getDB()\r\n\r\n2. Migration phase\r\nintroduced $pdo\r\n\r\n3. Current system\r\nfully PDO + bootstrap\r\n\r\nBUT:\r\n\r\nfiles