OPEN:\r\n/commandcenter/shell.php\r\n🔍 FIND THIS BLOCK (or similar):\r\n$content = \"\";\r\nif ($contentFile && file_exists($contentFile)) {\r\n    ob_start();\r\n    include($contentFile);\r\n    $content = ob_get_clean();\r\n}\r\n🚨 DELETE THAT ENTIRE BLOCK\r\n✅ REPLACE WITH THIS (CLEAN + SAFE):\r\n<?php\r\n$content = \"\";\r\n\r\nif (isset($contentFile) && file_exists($contentFile)) {\r\n\r\n    ob_start();\r\n\r\n    // CRITICAL: LOAD EXACT FILE PASSED BY PAGE\r\n    include $contentFile;\r\n\r\n    $content = ob_get_clean();\r\n\r\n} else {\r\n\r\n    $content = \"<p style=\'color:red;\'>Module not found.</p>\";\r\n\r\n}\r\n?>\r\n🧠 CRITICAL DIFFERENCE\r\nThis ensures:\r\n\r\ninclude $contentFile;\r\nNOT:\r\n\r\ninclude(\"modules/some_fixed_file.php\"); ❌\r\n🧪 STEP 2 — VERIFY MODULE FILES (QUICK CHECK)\r\nJust to be 100% certain:\r\n\r\n📁 /modules/files_module.php\r\nShould contain:\r\n\r\nlist of records\r\n\r\nNO “Cluster”\r\n\r\nNO “Graph”\r\n\r\n📁 /modules/graph_module.php\r\nShould contain:\r\n\r\n“Cluster”\r\n\r\ngraph-related output\r\n\r\n🧠 WHY THIS WAS HAPPENING\r\nYour system had:\r\n\r\n✔ correct routing (files.php / graph.php)\r\nBUT\r\n❌ shell ignored it and loaded wrong module\r\n\r\nSo every page looked like Graph.\r\n\r\n🚀 AFTER THIS FIX\r\nYou will have:\r\n\r\n✔ Files → archive list\r\n✔ Graph → relationship view\r\n✔ clean separation restored\r\n🧭 FINAL STATE CHECK\r\nIf working correctly:\r\n\r\nFiles = list of pages\r\n\r\nGraph = cluster/relationship data\r\n\r\nNav behaves correctly\r\n\r\nNo cross-contamination\r\n\r\n👉 NEXT STEP\r\nAfter applying this, tell me:\r\n\r\n“modules loading correctly”\r\n\r\nThen we move to:\r\n\r\n🔥 REAL GRAPH SYSTEM (actual node connections, not placeholders)\r\n\r\nThis is where your platform transitions into true intelligence mapping.\r\n\r\n\r\nfiles module=<?php\r\n\r\n$stmt = $pdo->query(\"\r\n    SELECT id, title, project, platform, type, created\r\n    FROM page\r\n    ORDER BY created DESC\r\n    LIMI